---
/* EVERY COUNTRY MOVED INTO EVERY PLACE. David: «every country can just move
   to "places"? surely and summarise the same numbers there?» and then
   «collapse it».

   It had already become the same thing: once CountryCards.astro was shared,
   this page and the country directory on /places/ were one component reading
   one set of numbers, printed twice under two names. Two pages that cannot
   disagree are still two pages a reader has to choose between.

   NOT DELETED, REDIRECTED. This URL is in the site's own navigation history,
   in its sitemap, and — for all anyone here knows — in somebody's bookmarks
   and in a search index. Deleting it turns those into 404s to save one file.
   A static host has no 301 to offer, so the redirect is the two things a
   static page CAN do: a canonical link, which is what a search engine reads,
   and a meta refresh, which is what a person gets. */
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
const to = u("/places/");
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Every country — moved to Every place</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href={to} />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`0; url=${to}`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>Every country is now part of <a href={to}>Every place</a> — the same
    countries, the same numbers, and the places underneath them.</p>
  </body>
</html>
